From 8e0d56c308e28e9463b5284f33aadf78390daf09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 06:52:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] system: Submit Log says that the names of Bluetooth devices
 become markers

The filter of the diagnostics now turns the names of the Bluetooth devices that BlueZ keeps into markers, in everything it filters; the two texts of Submit Log that list what becomes a marker say so.
---
 resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po | 4 ++--
 resources/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po | 8 ++++----
 resources/language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po | 8 ++++----
 resources/language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po | 8 ++++----
 4 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po b/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
index 00e0181..a1dfea9 100644
--- a/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
+++ b/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
@@ -1261,7 +1261,7 @@ msgid "Upload it to the paste service of LibreELEC"
 msgstr ""
 
 msgctxt "#32944"
-msgid "The log goes to paste.libreelec.tv, a service of the LibreELEC project, and is kept there under a short address that anyone who has it can read.[CR][CR]It goes through the same filter as a log that is kept on this system: the addresses of your network, serial numbers and the names of your Wi-Fi networks and of this system become markers, and the paths of addresses, the names of films and searches, and what the filter takes for a key or a password are taken out. It still tells which add-ons you have and what kind of video was played, and it names your disks and your displays. No filter knows every key.[CR][CR]This is not LibreELEC's build, and Team LibreELEC does not support it: the address is for whoever helps you with this build."
+msgid "The log goes to paste.libreelec.tv, a service of the LibreELEC project, and is kept there under a short address that anyone who has it can read.[CR][CR]It goes through the same filter as a log that is kept on this system: the addresses of your network, serial numbers and the names of your Wi-Fi networks, of your Bluetooth devices and of this system become markers, and the paths of addresses, the names of films and searches, and what the filter takes for a key or a password are taken out. It still tells which add-ons you have and what kind of video was played, and it names your disks and your displays. No filter knows every key.[CR][CR]This is not LibreELEC's build, and Team LibreELEC does not support it: the address is for whoever helps you with this build."
 msgstr ""
 
 msgctxt "#32945"
@@ -1273,7 +1273,7 @@ msgid "The log is kept on this system, and nothing was sent:"
 msgstr ""
 
 msgctxt "#32947"
-msgid "It is what an upload would send, after the filter of the diagnostics: the addresses of your network, serial numbers and the names of your Wi-Fi networks and of this system become markers, each address is cut down to its server, the names of films and searches and what the filter takes for a key or a password are taken out, and the lines that are too long for it are left out. No filter knows every key: read it before you give it to anyone.[CR][CR]To take it from here: copy it to a USB drive with the file manager (add the home folder as a source: the log is in its folder logfiles), read the share Logfiles if file sharing (Samba) is on, or use SSH."
+msgid "It is what an upload would send, after the filter of the diagnostics: the addresses of your network, serial numbers and the names of your Wi-Fi networks, of your Bluetooth devices and of this system become markers, each address is cut down to its server, the names of films and searches and what the filter takes for a key or a password are taken out, and the lines that are too long for it are left out. No filter knows every key: read it before you give it to anyone.[CR][CR]To take it from here: copy it to a USB drive with the file manager (add the home folder as a source: the log is in its folder logfiles), read the share Logfiles if file sharing (Samba) is on, or use SSH."
 msgstr ""
 
